<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Squire Reading Stack 3: Simple Biographies</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@picocss/pico@2/css/pico.min.css" />
    <style>
      body {
        max-width: 880px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 32px 80px;
        position: relative;
        box-sizing: border-box;
        font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;
        background-color: #ffffff;
        color: #000000;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }
      h1,
      h2,
      h3,
      h4,
      h5,
      h6 {
        color: #000000;
        font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;
        font-weight: bold;
        margin-bottom: 16px;
      }
      h1 {
        text-align: center;
        font-size: 2.2rem;
        border-bottom: 2px solid #000;
        padding-bottom: 10px;
      }
      h2 {
        font-size: 1.8rem;
        margin-top: 0;
      }
      h3 {
        font-size: 1.3rem;
        margin-top: 24px;
        margin-bottom: 8px;
        text-decoration: underline;
      }
      p {
        margin-bottom: 16px;
        text-align: justify;
      }
      ul {
        margin-bottom: 16px;
        padding-left: 40px;
      }
      li {
        margin-bottom: 8px;
      }
      .intro-section {
        margin-bottom: 40px;
      }
      .biography-section {
        margin-top: 40px;
        break-before: page;
        page-break-before: always;
      }
      .key-facts-box {
        border: 1px solid #000000;
        padding: 16px 24px;
        margin: 24px 0;
        background-color: #fdfdfd;
      }
      .key-facts-box h4 {
        margin-top: 0;
        margin-bottom: 12px;
        font-size: 1.2rem;
        text-align: center;
      }
      .footer-note {
        margin-top: 60px;
        border-top: 1px solid #000;
        padding-top: 16px;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        font-style: italic;
        text-align: center;
      }
      hr {
        border: 0;
        border-top: 1px solid #000;
        margin: 40px 0;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="intro-section">
      <h1>Squire Reading Stack 3: Simple Biographies</h1>
      <p>
        <strong>Introduction:</strong> Welcome to the third reading stack for Squire School. This document introduces
        the key historical figures that every Squire must know.
      </p>
      <p>
        <em
          >Note: These biographies support Squire reading, memory work, timeline review, and board preparation. They are
          designed to be studied carefully alongside your weekly lessons.</em
        >
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Biography 1: Hugh de Payns -->
    <div class="biography-section">
      <h2>Hugh de Payns</h2>

      <h3>Who Was This Person?</h3>
      <p>
        Hugh de Payns is the founder most closely linked with the order. He and his first companions established the
        group to serve a specific mission.
      </p>

      <h3>Why This Person Matters in Squire School</h3>
      <p>
        Hugh de Payns matters because he is directly connected to why the order began. Learning about him helps Squires
        understand the foundational purpose of the order and the importance of its first companions.
      </p>

      <h3>Where This Person Fits in the Timeline</h3>
      <p>
        He fits at the very beginning of the order's history. The founding under Hugh de Payns occurred around 1119 or
        1120, which was after the First Crusade (1095–1099).
      </p>

      <div class="key-facts-box">
        <h4>Key Facts to Remember</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Founder most closely linked with the order.</li>
          <li>Founded the order around 1119 or 1120.</li>
          <li>Acted alongside the first companions.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h3>Remember This</h3>
      <p>Hugh de Payns is the founder most closely linked with the order's beginnings around 1119 or 1120.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Biography 2: Baldwin II -->
    <div class="biography-section">
      <h2>Baldwin II</h2>

      <h3>Who Was This Person?</h3>
      <p>Baldwin II was the king of Jerusalem during the early days of the order.</p>

      <h3>Why This Person Matters in Squire School</h3>
      <p>
        Baldwin II matters because he is connected with the early Templars and the Kingdom of Jerusalem. Knowing his
        role helps Squires understand the political setting in which the order operated.
      </p>

      <h3>Where This Person Fits in the Timeline</h3>
      <p>
        He fits in the early timeline around the founding of the order in 1119 or 1120, establishing the order's
        connection to the Kingdom of Jerusalem.
      </p>

      <div class="key-facts-box">
        <h4>Key Facts to Remember</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>King of Jerusalem.</li>
          <li>Connected to the early Templars.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h3>Remember This</h3>
      <p>Baldwin II was the king of Jerusalem who was connected with the early Templars.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Biography 3: Bernard of Clairvaux -->
    <div class="biography-section">
      <h2>Bernard of Clairvaux</h2>

      <h3>Who Was This Person?</h3>
      <p>Bernard of Clairvaux was an important church figure and a major supporter of the order.</p>

      <h3>Why This Person Matters in Squire School</h3>
      <p>
        He matters because he was an important supporter of the order after its founding. While he was not a founder
        himself, his support helped the order gain recognition.
      </p>

      <h3>Where This Person Fits in the Timeline</h3>
      <p>
        He fits into the timeline after the founding, particularly around the time of the Council of Troyes (around 1128
        or 1129), when the order received formal support.
      </p>

      <div class="key-facts-box">
        <h4>Key Facts to Remember</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Important supporter of the order.</li>
          <li>Provided support after the order was already founded.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h3>Remember This</h3>
      <p>Bernard of Clairvaux was an important supporter of the order after its founding.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Biography 4: Innocent II -->
    <div class="biography-section">
      <h2>Innocent II</h2>

      <h3>Who Was This Person?</h3>
      <p>Innocent II was a pope who recognized and supported the order's mission.</p>

      <h3>Why This Person Matters in Squire School</h3>
      <p>
        He matters because he granted major privileges to the order. This papal support was a significant event in the
        order's history.
      </p>

      <h3>Where This Person Fits in the Timeline</h3>
      <p>Pope Innocent II fits into the timeline in the year 1139, which is when he granted these major privileges.</p>

      <div class="key-facts-box">
        <h4>Key Facts to Remember</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>He was a pope.</li>
          <li>Granted major privileges to the order.</li>
          <li>Acted in the year 1139.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h3>Remember This</h3>
      <p>Pope Innocent II granted major privileges to the order in 1139.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Biography 5: Philip IV -->
    <div class="biography-section">
      <h2>Philip IV</h2>

      <h3>Who Was This Person?</h3>
      <p>Philip IV was a ruler in France during the later years of the order.</p>

      <h3>Why This Person Matters in Squire School</h3>
      <p>
        He matters because he is the ruler who ordered the arrests of the Templars in France, marking the beginning of
        the order's major crisis.
      </p>

      <h3>Where This Person Fits in the Timeline</h3>
      <p>
        Philip IV fits into the timeline in 1307, the year he ordered the arrests. This occurred after the fall of Acre
        in 1291.
      </p>

      <div class="key-facts-box">
        <h4>Key Facts to Remember</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Ruler in France.</li>
          <li>Ordered the arrests of the Templars.</li>
          <li>The arrests took place in 1307.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h3>Remember This</h3>
      <p>Philip IV was the ruler who ordered the arrests of the Templars in France in 1307.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Biography 6: Clement V -->
    <div class="biography-section">
      <h2>Clement V</h2>

      <h3>Who Was This Person?</h3>
      <p>Clement V was the pope during the final years of the order's existence.</p>

      <h3>Why This Person Matters in Squire School</h3>
      <p>
        He matters because he is the pope who officially suppressed the order, bringing its formal history to a close.
      </p>

      <h3>Where This Person Fits in the Timeline</h3>
      <p>
        Pope Clement V fits into the timeline in 1312, which is the year he suppressed the order (five years after the
        arrests in 1307).
      </p>

      <div class="key-facts-box">
        <h4>Key Facts to Remember</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>He was a pope.</li>
          <li>Suppressed the order.</li>
          <li>The suppression happened in 1312.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h3>Remember This</h3>
      <p>Pope Clement V suppressed the order in 1312.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Biography 7: Jacques de Molay -->
    <div class="biography-section">
      <h2>Jacques de Molay</h2>

      <h3>Who Was This Person?</h3>
      <p>Jacques de Molay was the last Grand Master of the order.</p>

      <h3>Why This Person Matters in Squire School</h3>
      <p>
        He matters because he is connected to the very end of the order. Understanding his role helps Squires complete
        their knowledge of the order's historical timeline.
      </p>

      <h3>Where This Person Fits in the Timeline</h3>
      <p>
        He fits at the end of the historical timeline. Jacques de Molay was executed in 1314, after the suppression of
        the order in 1312.
      </p>

      <div class="key-facts-box">
        <h4>Key Facts to Remember</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>The last Grand Master.</li>
          <li>Connected to the end of the order.</li>
          <li>Executed in 1314.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h3>Remember This</h3>
      <p>Jacques de Molay was the last Grand Master and was executed in 1314.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Review Section -->
    <div class="biography-section">
      <h2>Names Every Squire Should Know</h2>
      <p>Review this simple list of the seven key figures and their most important historical actions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Hugh de Payns:</strong> The founder most closely linked with the order (around 1119 or 1120).</li>
        <li><strong>Baldwin II:</strong> The king of Jerusalem connected with the early Templars.</li>
        <li><strong>Bernard of Clairvaux:</strong> An important supporter of the order after its founding.</li>
        <li><strong>Innocent II:</strong> The pope who granted major privileges to the order in 1139.</li>
        <li><strong>Philip IV:</strong> The ruler who ordered the arrests of the Templars in France in 1307.</li>
        <li><strong>Clement V:</strong> The pope who suppressed the order in 1312.</li>
        <li><strong>Jacques de Molay:</strong> The last Grand Master, executed in 1314.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <div class="footer-note">
      <p>
        This handout is based on official Squire School curriculum materials and should be studied with timeline sheets,
        school handouts, and supervised class discussion.
      </p>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
